data receiver_retention_legs_never_reddened_by_a_measured_control: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "receiver_retention_legs_never_reddened_by_a_measured_control" as NonEmptyStr,

  rung: RungRead { found_at: FoundBelowTheLadder, standing: BelowCeiling { current: FoundBelowTheLadder, ceiling: StructurallyGuaranteed, blocker: ClimbableButUnbuilt, trigger_capability: "EVALUABLE, NOT A DATE. In one heavy-slot acquisition on a gunbc binary whose sha256 is printed from disk, run `gunbc test //test/claim/algebra_receiver_retention_carrier_witness:<leg>` for the named leg under a RedProbe break (gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_status RedProbe, never-merged probe branch) keyed to that leg's named retention mechanism, with the discriminating pair of gunbc test run in the same acquisition to prove the break is causal. The trigger FIRES for one leg when that leg's verdict line reads DID NOT HOLD with eval_steps greater than zero and its own rc 1, while the pair still splits. A fired leg gains control standing: its carrier comment is deleted, it returns to a guarantee witness as a control leg, and it leaves this row's population. The row retires when the population reaches zero. A break that reddens none of the four legs satisfies nothing; deleting a leg satisfies nothing; a date satisfies nothing." } },

  receipts: [
    "INVALID STATE: four receiver-coverage legs assert that a type carried through a pattern or fold position survives to method lookup -- nested_generic_pattern_still_expands_for_lookup (a doubly-nested coproduct pattern: ApplicationBoxed { value: RowsPresent { rows } } must expand so the inner rows binding instantiates the any-callback's receiver), whole_value_pattern_retains_application_for_later_destructuring (the whole value bound by `bound` must retain the application for the later inner match), matched_collection_retains_receiver_type_argument (the field's resolved type carries FreeMonoid's nominal argument outside its expanded body: binding the field must not substitute that body's Empty member for ApplicationRow when instantiating the any callback), and folded_structural_collection_can_reverse (reverse() is a ReceiverSelf method and must resolve against the list produced by fold_list, with other profile methods not contributing their evidence requirements to the lookup). None has ever reddened under any measured control, so none is a control: the pass can come from the retention machinery OR from the receiver being admitted by key with the shape never judged, and the leg cannot tell the two apart. A coverage leg that greens whether or not the compiler is right about the position it names enrols the admitted-by-key residue as an asset; gunbc.design_argument::guarantee_ladder (no untracked stall) requires such a site to carry a declared row with a bounded trigger rather than stand silently in a guarantee witness.",

    "MEASURED, NOT ASSUMED, 2026-11-27, session lively-fox-770, srv1 (BOOT c095c0cd-1eaa-4bc7-861d-2bd9756c2bc4), legs executed by name on the main-built gunbc (sha256 printed from disk in the acquisition log): all four legs HELD outcome=Pass. Two RedProbe breaks were then run against the same leg set. BREAK 1 (probe v1, silencing the annotated let-bound type propagation) reddened 0 of the 6 first_slice legs including these four. BREAK 2 (probe v3, silencing the evidence census at BOTH layers -- src/v1/04_types.dag `let evidence_diags = if false` plus the stage0 mirror v1_compiler_infer_types.rs, probe commit c9dbea0eaf2, never merged) reddened the expansion-evidence decider (expansion_receiver_raises_the_evidence_diagnostic DID NOT HOLD outcome=ExitFailure code=1 eval_steps=447, own rc 1, while nominal_receiver_raises_no_evidence_diagnostic stayed HELD -- the pair split proving the run causally instrumented) while these four legs stayed HELD outcome=Pass in the same acquisitions. The four therefore have zero control standing as a MEASURED property, not an assumed one; the acquisitions are named in the PR evidence comments for method-receiver-normalization (#17138).",

    "WHAT THE WITNESS KEEPS AFTER THE MOVE: the discriminating pair, and only the discriminating pair, stays in the guarantee witnesses -- test.claim.algebra_receiver_alias_witness keeps its three refusal fixtures each with its own cause (alias_return_is_a_refusal_fixture, alias_field_is_a_refusal_fixture, alias_field_refusal_is_a_no_observation_with_its_own_cause); test.claim.algebra_receiver_alias_agreement_witness keeps bogus_method_refuses_under_both_spellings REFUSED against nominal_return_is_accepted ACCEPTED; test.claim.algebra_expansion_evidence_witness keeps the pair split (expansion raises the evidence diagnostic, nominal stays silent). The four coverage legs continue to EXECUTE, but from this row's carrier module test.claim.algebra_receiver_retention_carrier_witness, where each carries this row's bounded flip trigger in its leg comment and goes red with the wall rather than being deleted silently. This row is the single home of the zero-standing fact for these four sites; it does not re-home any other row's defect: the lambda-parameter receiver cause is discharged (first_slice, green on main), the coproduct-payload, optional-cardinality and brand-alias-LEAF causes are declared on the gunbc#7484 frontier roster, and the alias-return silent acceptance is carried by its GuaranteeProbeRow in gunbc.guarantee_probe_corpus.",
  ],

  evidence: [
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "test.claim.algebra_receiver_retention_carrier_witness", decl_name: "nested_generic_pattern_still_expands_for_lookup", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "test.claim.algebra_receiver_retention_carrier_witness", decl_name: "whole_value_pattern_retains_application_for_later_destructuring", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "test.claim.algebra_receiver_retention_carrier_witness", decl_name: "matched_collection_retains_receiver_type_argument", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "test.claim.algebra_receiver_retention_carrier_witness", decl_name: "folded_structural_collection_can_reverse", field: WholeDeclaration },
  ],
}
